# Netlify reads this file from the root of the published directory (_book/).
# It is copied there by `resources:` in _quarto.yml — see the note there.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#
# On 15 Aug 2026 a corrected page kept serving its previous version through
# repeated reloads, including DevTools "Empty Cache and Hard Reload". That
# clears the BROWSER's copy, so the fact that it changed nothing is the whole
# diagnosis: the stale copy was not in the browser. Netlify was reporting
#
#     cache-status: "Netlify Edge"; hit; ttl=31535985
#
# on the HTML — a year-long time to live at the edge. Appending ?v=2 produced
# the new page instantly, which confirms it: a different query string is a
# different cache key at the edge, so that request missed the stale entry and
# went to origin. The origin was correct the entire time.
#
# This had cost three review cycles before it was diagnosed, each one looking
# like "the fix did not work" when the fix had already shipped.
#
# THE TWO HEADERS ARE NOT THE SAME KNOB
#
# Cache-Control            governs the visitor's browser.
# Netlify-CDN-Cache-Control governs Netlify's edge, and takes precedence there.
#
# The site was already sending `Cache-Control: public,max-age=0,must-revalidate`,
# which is correct and was never the problem. Only the second header reaches the
# edge, so only the second header could have fixed this.
#
# `no-cache` does NOT mean "do not store". It means "revalidate before serving".
# Both layers still keep the file and still answer with 304 Not Modified when
# nothing changed, so repeat visits stay fast. What it removes is the ability to
# serve a stale copy without asking.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Netlify-CDN-Cache-Control: no-cache

# Quarto's bundled libraries carry their version in the directory name
# (bootstrap-5.x, quarto-html, and so on), so any change to them changes the
# URL. Those are safe to cache hard and never go stale.
/site_libs/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Netlify-CDN-Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
